  "text": "GANGSTAS PARADISE (Sleeper) \u2014 Higgins, Flowers and Downs all still trending to play; no formal tags until Tuesday's practice report \u2014 lineup set\nDo now: nothing \u2014 lineup is set\nLocks next 24h: none \u2014 first kickoff is Fri 5:00 PM PT (Herbert, Hampton vs KC, S\u00e3o Paulo)\nLineup, by kickoff: Herbert (QB) and Hampton (RB), Fri 5:00 PM PT vs KC \u2014 no news, both in. Chase Brown (RB), Higgins (WR, Q \u2014 heel contusion; Taylor called it minor and Higgins reportedly ran the hill Wednesday, a good sign), Flowers (WR, Q \u2014 lower-body/quad, back at practice Thursday, Minter optimistic for Week 1), Strange (TE), Tuten (FLEX RB \u2014 sent home sick 9/2, no update since but JAX doesn't kick off until Sunday so no Week 1 risk yet), Downs (FLEX WR, Q \u2014 calf, \"very minor\" per Downs himself, trending toward playing), and JAX DEF all kick off Sun 10:00 AM PT. Aubrey (K) closes it out Sun 5:20 PM PT @ NYG. None of these are formal designations yet \u2014 Indianapolis/Cincinnati/Baltimore's first official injury reports land with Tuesday's practice. If Higgins is out, start Diggs. If Flowers is out, start Diggs. If Downs is out, start Diggs; if two of Higgins/Flowers/Downs are out, Diggs then Michael Wilson. If Tuten is out, start Woody Marks.\n\nGAME OF THROWS (Yahoo) \u2014 39% underdog vs GIBBBBBYYYY; no new screenshots since Friday night, lineup unchanged \u2014 lineup set\nDo now: nothing \u2014 lineup is set\nLocks next 24h: none \u2014 first kickoff is Wed 5:20 PM PT (Myers vs NE)\nLineup, by kickoff: Myers (K), Wed 5:20 PM PT vs NE \u2014 no news, in. Stafford (QB) and 49ers DEF, Thu 5:35 PM PT @ LAR in Melbourne \u2014 Stafford no news; McCaffrey (SF's workhorse, not on your roster but drives this game's script) had a full practice and Shanahan says he'd play if it were the regular season, so no game-flow risk to your DEF. Chase Brown (RB), Etienne (RB), Judkins (W/R/T), G. Wilson (WR) and P. Washington (WR) all kick off Sun 10:00 AM PT \u2014 no changes, Etienne still the clean NO lead with Kamara out. Pickens (WR) and Likely (TE) close it out Sun 5:20 PM PT @ NYG / vs DAL \u2014 no news, both in. No Qs on this roster, no contingencies needed.\n\nFYI: Chase Brown starts for you in both leagues; your JAX DEF (Sleeper) and Judkins' Browns (Yahoo) collide in the same CLE@JAX game; Sleeper opp AdufortheWin84's McCaffrey (full practice, on track) and Henderson (minor ankle tweak Monday, \"good to go\") are both trending healthy; Yahoo opp Arshdeep's three Qs (Jeanty, Nabers, LaPorta) are unresolved with no new reports since Friday. Michael Pittman Jr. has been traded to Pittsburgh \u2014 he's the Sleeper opponent's WR2 now, no current PIT injury news.\nData: Sleeper live \u00b7 Yahoo screenshots from 2026-09-05 (no fresher ones in Drive \u2014 send new screenshots once Yahoo posts its own Week 1 report, likely mid-week)",
